{
  "clause": "S290",
  "about": "AirPlay row, master and stored own volume. k = (zone/100)(master/100); level D = min(100, own x k); the row shows D rounded down with 0.01 of slack. Ops, applied in order to one speaker: own sets the stored own volume; row_move moves the row to R (sends D = R and stores own = R / k, or sends nothing at k = 0, marked sent false); tv_level is a level set on the speaker (D = tv_level, own = D / k); master moves the master and keeps own. After each step, level is the D the speaker gets (compare within 1e-6) and row is what the row shows.",
